+
+## What changed
+
+- Replaced the original Home wording and two-line layout with the reference's **“Portraits / worth / keeping.”** composition and supporting copy.
+- Replaced EB Garamond with licensed, self-hosted **Bodoni Moda** for the reference's stronger contrast and sharper editorial shapes.
+- Corrected desktop hero tracks, headline scale, photograph height, motif height and copy rhythm. Increased the header, interface type and booking controls to the selected reference’s relative scale; corrected the mobile Portfolio heading and feature-photo height. The real pinned hero remains `27-img-0297.jpg`.
+- Changed selected work to four monochrome tiles across desktop. All six curated images remain; the final pair spans two tracks. Mobile uses two columns. Original colour remains available through hover/lightbox; file bytes are intact.
+- Changed visible navigation to **Work / About / Sessions / Contact**. The real document routes and accessible Home link remain intact.
+- Rebuilt Portfolio around the reference introduction and feature photo. On mobile, the heading leads straight into the photograph and its caption. The underlying 30-frame gallery, actual order, packer and lightbox remain intact.
+- Rebuilt About as **“Behind the lens.”** introduction, actual photographer photo, separate landscape/biography section, and three brand-value blocks. No client is presented as the photographer.
+- Rebuilt Services around **“Sessions, with intention.”**, a curated real portrait, light bordered package cards, restrained recommendation styling, and monochrome card photography. Social remains R3,500; all deliverables and terms remain unchanged.
+- Rebuilt Contact with the mockup's three-line invitation, plain white form, supporting photograph and editorial contact details. The complete family frame is preserved rather than cutting off faces.
+- Replaced the white dropdown with the reference's **dark full-screen mobile navigation**, keeping focus trap/return, Escape, backdrop dismissal and desktop teardown.
+- Replaced the oversized legacy closing treatment with a smaller editorial booking band and the **“People. Places. Stories.”** footer.
+
+## Evidence and acceptance
+
+The updated `review/index.html` shows current before/after pages and source comparisons. Full final captures cover all five pages at 320/390/430/768/1024/1440/1920. `review/comparisons/home-primary-reference.jpg` is the combined selected-reference/implementation board.
+
+Automated checks validate functionality and responsive integrity; they do not grant visual approval. The revised screenshots are submitted for the owner's assessment. No merge or deployment is authorized by this report.
+
+## Remaining factual/asset constraints
+
+Real photographs must differ from the generated concept faces. The authentic photographer's pinned environmental portrait remains intact. Real business hours/location, all package benefits and terms, and all six curated Home images take precedence over abbreviated or illustrative prototype content. No Journal route, fake testimonials, telephone link or fabricated business claims are introduced.
